  "term": "convergent strabismus",
  "definition": "Convergent strabismus is an eye alignment problem in which the eyes turn inward too much, giving a cross-eyed appearance. It can happen when weakness or paralysis of the lateral rectus muscle makes one eye deviate inward during attempted gaze.",
